@meta
id: 16-19
title: Scenario — the cancellation email
chapter: 16
type: scenario
skills: buffer-switch, buffer-list, split-window, search-slash, open-o
par: 270
minutes: 12
vscode: five tabs, and the registry is the one you forget
open: order.provider.ts email.service.ts registry.ts customer.provider.ts errors.json

@brief
A ticket, not an exercise.

    ORD-467  Customers hear nothing when an order is cancelled. Send
             the order-cancelled email after the refund goes through.
             The email service plumbing landed last sprint; the call
             was never written, the template does not exist, and
             nobody registered the service.

Five buffers. Three change, two are there to read. Nothing tells you
which is which except the ticket and the code.

  1. `order.provider.ts` — `cancel` already has `emailService`
     injected. After the refund call and before the update, add:

         await this.emailService.send({
           customerId: order.customerId,
           template: 'order-cancelled',
         });

     with a blank line on either side of it.

  2. `email.service.ts` — `EmailTemplate` does not include
     `'order-cancelled'`. Append it to the union, last, before the
     semicolon.

  3. `registry.ts` — `EmailService` is imported and never registered.
     Add its registration as the last line of the file, in the same
     shape as the others.

  4. `customer.provider.ts` and `errors.json` — reference only. The
     email service takes a customer id, not an address, so the customer
     provider is not needed; check that yourself rather than taking
     the ticket's word for it. Neither file may change.

@keys
| `:b email` `:b reg` | by name, no list |
| `:sp name` | if you would rather see a reference beside the code |
| `Ctrl-^` | between the two you are alternating |
| `:ls` | `+` on anything you have changed and not written |
| `:wqa` | the exit |

@hints
Provider first: `/refund(` lands on the refund line. `o`, Enter for
the blank line, then the four lines. Autoindent handles the leading
spaces; type none.
--
`:b email`, `/password`, `$`, `i`, type ` | 'order-cancelled'`. The
`$` puts you on the semicolon and `i` inserts before it.
--
`:b reg`, `G`, `o`, the registration line. It is the same shape as
the line above it, so `yy` `p` and two `cw` is an alternative to
typing it.
--
Write before each hop unless `hidden` is on in your vimrc; `:ls` will
tell you what is still `+`. `:wqa` at the end regardless.

@solution
A reasonable route, buffer by buffer.

**order.provider.ts** — `/refund(` `Enter`, `o`, `Enter`, then the
four lines with Enter between them, `Esc`, `:w`.

**email.service.ts** — `:b email`, `/password` `Enter`, `$`, `i`,
` | 'order-cancelled'`, `Esc`, `:w`.

**registry.ts** — `:b reg`, `G`, `o`, the registration line, `Esc`.

**customer.provider.ts**, **errors.json** — `:b cust` or `:b err` to
look, `Ctrl-^` to come back, and nothing else.

`:wqa`.

About two hundred and forty keystrokes, and everything that is not
typed code is under thirty. The chapter's whole contribution to a job
like this is that the switching disappears: three files, three names,
and at no point did you look at a list or a strip of tabs to find one.

The other thing this one tests is restraint. Two of the five buffers
are open because a real ticket lands on a codebase, not on the three
files it mentions, and the habit of opening things to read them has
to coexist with the habit of not typing into them. `:ls` before
`:wqa` is the check: anything with a `+` that should not have one is a
`u` away from clean.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    await this.emailService.send({
      customerId: order.customerId,
      template: 'order-cancelled',
    });

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start email.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';

export type EmailTemplate = 'order-shipped' | 'password-reset';

@injectable()
export class EmailService {
  public async send(args: { customerId: string; template: EmailTemplate }) {
    return this.http.post(`/send`, args);
  }
}

@expected email.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';

export type EmailTemplate = 'order-shipped' | 'password-reset' | 'order-cancelled';

@injectable()
export class EmailService {
  public async send(args: { customerId: string; template: EmailTemplate }) {
    return this.http.post(`/send`, args);
  }
}

@start registry.ts
import { container } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderRepository } from '../domain/order/order.repository';
import { OrderProvider } from '../domain/order/order.provider';
import { OrderResolver } from '../domain/order/order.resolver';
import { CustomerRepository } from '../domain/customer/customer.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../domain/customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../infrastructure/services/email.service';

container.register('OrderRepository', { useClass: OrderRepository });
container.register('CustomerRepository', { useClass: CustomerRepository });
container.register('OrderProvider', { useClass: OrderProvider });
container.register('CustomerProvider', { useClass: CustomerProvider });
container.register('OrderResolver', { useClass: OrderResolver });
container.register('PaymentService', { useClass: PaymentService });

@expected registry.ts
import { container } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderRepository } from '../domain/order/order.repository';
import { OrderProvider } from '../domain/order/order.provider';
import { OrderResolver } from '../domain/order/order.resolver';
import { CustomerRepository } from '../domain/customer/customer.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../domain/customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../infrastructure/services/email.service';

container.register('OrderRepository', { useClass: OrderRepository });
container.register('CustomerRepository', { useClass: CustomerRepository });
container.register('OrderProvider', { useClass: OrderProvider });
container.register('CustomerProvider', { useClass: CustomerProvider });
container.register('OrderResolver', { useClass: OrderResolver });
container.register('PaymentService', { useClass: PaymentService });
container.register('EmailService', { useClass: EmailService });

@start customer.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { CustomerRepository } from './customer.repository';

@injectable()
export class CustomerProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(CustomerRepository) protected customerRepository: CustomerRepository,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const customer = await this.customerRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!customer) {
      throw exception('CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return customer;
  }
}

